<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Caw Ridge</name>
<Placemark><name>Waypoint</name><description>The point this guide is built around. It sits in a high bowl with a short view.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.390728,54.062707,1991</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G1 glassing point</name><description>Sees 6.8 km2 of open ground within 3 km. 1.2 km from the waypoint, bearing 183 true.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.391739,54.052100,2026</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G2 glassing point</name><description>Sees 6.4 km2 of open ground within 3 km. 5.5 km from the waypoint, bearing 140 true.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.336665,54.024868,2160</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G3 glassing point</name><description>Sees 5.5 km2 of open ground within 3 km. 4.9 km from the waypoint, bearing 110 true.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.321061,54.047517,1918</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G4 glassing point</name><description>Sees 4.9 km2 of open ground within 3 km. 6.4 km from the waypoint, bearing 136 true.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.322896,54.021631,2008</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G5 glassing point</name><description>Sees 4.6 km2 of open ground within 3 km. 2.4 km from the waypoint, bearing 177 true.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.388985,54.041047,1950</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G6 glassing point</name><description>Sees 4.5 km2 of open ground within 3 km. 2.4 km from the waypoint, bearing 249 true.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.424783,54.055065,2017</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G7 glassing point</name><description>Sees 3.0 km2 of open ground within 3 km. 3.9 km from the waypoint, bearing 216 true.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.426160,54.034037,2021</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G8 glassing point</name><description>Sees 2.8 km2 of open ground within 3 km. 4.4 km from the waypoint, bearing 279 true.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.457369,54.068807,2020</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>End of mapped track</name><description>Where the track drawn in OpenStreetMap stops. Riders report old roads along most of the ridge line.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.389988,54.068003,2002</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Caw Ridge turnoff</name><description>Leave the gravel here. 8.1 km of old exploration road climbs to the ridge. A staging area is reported at the turnoff.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.323930,54.095806,1284</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Beaverdam Road turnoff</name><description>Leave Highway 40 here, 8 km north of Grande Cache. The road crosses coal mine property: stay on Beaverdam Road.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.176448,53.924359,973</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Grande Cache</name><description>Fuel, groceries, lodging, tourism centre. Last services.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.118600,53.888100,1257</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Grande Cache hospital</name><description>Grande Cache Community Health Complex, 10200 Shand Avenue. Emergency department open 24 hours. Helipad.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.118909,53.890938,1261</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Fuel: Fas Gas</name><description>Fuel in Grande Cache.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.113488,53.888584,1260</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Fuel: Petro-Canada</name><description>Fuel in Grande Cache.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.115951,53.891731,1266</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sheep Creek campground</name><description>Provincial recreation area on Highway 40, 25 km north of Grande Cache. Boat launch.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.011219,54.062174,902</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Smoky River South campground</name><description>Provincial recreation area, 22 unserviced sites. Usually open to Thanksgiving.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.158516,53.890360,961</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sulphur Gates campground</name><description>Provincial recreation area and Willmore staging. 11 sites, open all year. Firearm discharge permit rules apply here.</description><Point><coordinates>-119.186183,53.850132,1011</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
